P(X \geq 6) = \sum_{k=6}^{10} \binom{10}{k} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^k \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10-k} = \sum_{k=6}^{10} \binom{10}{k} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10}
\] \[
= \left(\binom{10}{6} + \binom{10}{7} + \binom{10}{8} + \binom{10}{9} + \binom{10}{10}\right) \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10}
\] \[
= \left(210 + 120 + 45 + 10 + 1\right) \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10} = \frac{386}{1024} = \frac{193}{512}
